      {
        "option": "Add project-specific guarantee or submission keywords",
        "decision": "rejected",
        "reason": "It would tune to observed Development cases instead of fixing the general evidence-relation problem."
      },
      {
        "option": "Move directly to GraphRAG, Neo4j or long-term memory",
        "decision": "rejected",
        "reason": "The missing Gold was already in the same candidate pool; graph storage and cross-session memory do not solve Top-5 selection loss."
      },
      {
        "option": "Design an anchor-preserving coverage selector on the same fixed Development pool",
        "decision": "selected",
        "reason": "It directly addresses the observed selection loss without consuming another Holdout."
      }
    ],
    "next_optimization_direction": [
      "Keep RET-CANDIDATE-COVERAGE-002 rejected and keep the production flag disabled.",
      "Create RET-CANDIDATE-COVERAGE-003 with one general variable: preserve high-confidence baseline anchors before using fact coverage to fill remaining Top-5 positions.",
      "Do not treat generic term overlap as answer coverage; require deterministic alignment of target entity, relation or attribute before a coverage candidate may replace an anchor.",
      "Use the same frozen 38-question Development pool and the same project-level gates; do not run Taifeng, Lancheng or Huizhou.",
